cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReviewDesk in a review, please cite it as below."
title: "ReviewDesk: free software for the record-handling stages of a systematic review"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Humphries
    given-names: Chris
version: "1.3.1"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/cphumphries/ReviewDesk"
url: "https://github.com/cphumphries/ReviewDesk"
keywords:
  - systematic review
  - screening
  - PRISMA 2020
  - PRISMA-S
  - GRADE
  - evidence synthesis
abstract: >-
  ReviewDesk runs the record-handling stages of a systematic review for a small team on their own computers, with
  the review in a shared folder: search logging, import and de-duplication, title and abstract screening with a
  calibration round, an agreement sample and an optional AI second screener that never excludes, full-text review,
  data extraction, risk of bias, GRADE certainty ratings, and the PRISMA 2020 flow diagram and reporting files.
